#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:13
msgid "What is BuddyPress Activity Filter?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:14
msgid ""
"It gives you control over the BuddyPress activity stream. You can hide "
"activity types you do not want members to see, and choose which filter is "
"selected by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:17
msgid "How do I set a default filter for all activity streams?"
msgstr "Comment définir un filtre par défaut pour tous les flux d'activité ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:18
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Navigate to the Default Filters tab and select your preferred default "
#| "filter from the dropdown. This filter will be applied automatically when "
#| "users visit the activity stream."
msgid ""
"Open the Default Filters tab and pick a default from the site-wide dropdown. "
"It applies automatically the first time someone loads the activity stream."
msgstr ""
"Accédez à l'onglet Filtres par défaut et sélectionnez le filtre par défaut "
"de votre choix dans la liste déroulante. Ce filtre sera appliqué "
"automatiquement lorsque les utilisateurs visiteront le flux d'activités."

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:21
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Can I set different default filters for profile pages?"
msgid "Can I set a different default filter for profiles?"
msgstr ""
"Puis-je définir différents filtres par défaut pour les pages de profil ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:22
msgid ""
"Yes. The Default Filters tab has a separate profile dropdown so member "
"profile streams can default to something different from the site-wide stream."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:25
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "How do I hide specific activity types from users?"
msgid "How do I hide specific activity types?"
msgstr "Comment masquer des types d'activités spécifiques aux utilisateurs ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:26
msgid ""
"Use the Hidden Activities tab and check the types you want to hide. Hidden "
"types are removed from streams and the filter dropdown. Core status updates "
"and replies cannot be hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:29
msgid "Does hiding a type delete those activities?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:30
msgid ""
"No. Hiding excludes the type from the activity query, so those entries stop "
"appearing immediately and come back if you unhide the type. They stay "
"visible on the WordPress Activity screen so you can still moderate them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:33
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Why are some activities not showing up in the filter?"
msgid "Why are some activities missing from the filter?"
msgstr "Pourquoi certaines activités n'apparaissent-elles pas dans le filtre ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:34
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Check the Hidden Activities tab to ensure the activity type is not "
#| "hidden. Also, some activity types may not have a filter option if they "
#| "are system activities or if they have been disabled by other plugins."
msgid ""
"Check the Hidden Activities tab to confirm the type is not hidden. Some "
"system activity types may also be unavailable if another plugin has disabled "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Vérifiez l'onglet Activités cachées pour vous assurer que le type d'activité "
"n'est pas caché. De plus, certains types d'activités peuvent ne pas avoir "
"d'option de filtrage s'il s'agit d'activités système ou si elles ont été "
"désactivées par d'autres plugins."

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:37
msgid "Is this plugin compatible with BuddyBoss Platform?"
msgstr "Ce plugin est-il compatible avec la plateforme BuddyBoss ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:38
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "BuddyPress Activity Filter is designed specifically for BuddyPress. "
#| "BuddyBoss Platform includes its own built-in activity filtering features, "
#| "so this plugin is not needed and may not be fully compatible with "
#| "BuddyBoss."
msgid ""
"No. This plugin is built for BuddyPress. BuddyBoss Platform has its own "
"activity filtering, so this plugin is not needed and is not fully compatible "
"with it."
msgstr ""
"BuddyPress Activity Filter est conçu spécifiquement pour BuddyPress. La "
"plateforme BuddyBoss comprend ses propres fonctions de filtrage d'activité, "
"ce plugin n'est donc pas nécessaire et peut ne pas être entièrement "
"compatible avec BuddyBoss."

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:41
msgid "How do filters affect activity stream performance?"
msgstr ""
"Comment les filtres affectent-ils les performances du flux d'activité ?"

#: includes/admin/views/faq.php:42
msgid ""
"Filtering happens at the database query level using BuddyPress core "
"mechanisms, so it stays efficient even on large activity streams."
msgstr ""

